A||||4||JSocha||Warning to anyone who may receive an EMAIL from me||||4||
Z||000000||JSocha||05-31-2001||11:12 AM||||Our purchasing department received an EMAIL from one of their vendors here at Rugby Manufacturing Company with a virus on it which attacks anyones address book.<P>If you suddenly receive an email from me with the following statement:<P><B>&gt; Take a look to the attachment.</B><P>DO NOT OPEN IT!  DELETE IT!  That is the Virus.<P>These files end in *.pif, *.scr and/or *.pif.scr and contain the virus.<P>I just opened my email client to check my email and send and receive messages, and BAM!  within two seconds it went through my entire ADDRESS BOOK and sent out this message with that statement to everyone on my list.<P>THIS IS NOT A HOAX and is being written by me to alert any of you on this forum that I may have posted in my email address book and/or had contacted directly off line.<P>This virus also passed by ours as well as our ISP's virus detection software and after it was to late.<P>Respectfully posted,<BR>Jeff Socha<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||Cheever2||05-31-2001||11:15 AM||||I thought that wasn't supposed to start until tomorrow.  j/k<P>Thanks for the tip.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||JSocha||05-31-2001||11:50 AM||||Update!<P>Currently scanning my computer with NORTON Anti-Virus here at work.  However, it apparently only attacks and sends out emails to any UNREAD or UNOPENED Email that you may have.<P>It was found on our PURCHASING Computer to attack the following files:<P><B>KERN32.EXE  C:\WINDOWS\SYSTEM</B><BR>(Update:  BACKDOOR.TROJAN)<P><B>HKSDLL.DLL  C:\WINDOWS\SYSTEM</B><BR>(Update:  ????)<P><B>INETD.EXE   C:\WINDOWS</B><BR>(Update:  W32BadTrans.13312@mm)<BR>================================<BR>I will post what specific VIRUS's to look for once Norton has had it's chance to scan my computer.  We are also trying to determine here at work why our EMAIL server Anti-Virus software did not stop this as well as the Anti-Virus programs loaded at individual PC's here at work.  It only found them after it happened!<P>Sorry for any inconvience guys!  This came as an unexpected surprise to me when over 906 emails suddenly got dumped into my OUTBOX in a flash and were being sent out.<P>Only good thing about this, is all those darn unsolicited P*RN emails we can not "unsubscribe" from that we get are going to get their just deserve!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Jeff Socha<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 05-31-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000003||Raydar||05-31-2001||01:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>...Only good thing about this, is all those darn unsolicited P*RN emails we can not "unsubscribe" from that we get are going to get their just deserve!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Jeff Socha<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL!!!<P>Thanks for the "heads up". It seems like the virus writers are always about a week ahead of the folks who write the antivirus software. We've actually been very lucky where I work. Last one that really got us was the Love Bug virus. And we were lucky. It nailed many other companies MUCH worse.<BR>We've learned a bunch, since that happened.<P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000004||JSocha||05-31-2001||04:28 PM||||Status:<P>Well, found out the BACKDOOR TROJAN is a worm virus.<P>It places the above listed files onto your computer, which don't exsist in the first place, and creates a Registry entry for KERN32.EXE to launch.  The DLL file is a password capture program which tries to send passwords and an IP back to the author which is apparently sent by the INETD.EXE file.<P>If anyone gets nailed with this, it only sends out the virus based on UNOPENED/UNREAD emails.<P>The following link will tell you more if it hits any of you and/or someone you know:<P> <A HREF="http://www.trusecure.com/html/tspub/hypeorhot/index.shtml#w32pokemon" TARGET=_blank>http://www.trusecure.com/html/tspub/hypeorhot/index.shtml#w32pokemon</A><BR> <A HREF="http://vil.mcafee.com/dispVirus.asp?virus_k=99069&" TARGET=_blank>http://vil.mcafee.com/dispVirus.asp?virus_k=99069&</A> <P><BR>Anyways, computer is back to normal now.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 05-31-2001).]||||reg||1
